# Wild Unraveling's other additional cost: with an Ornithopter to blight, Bot2 still pays {1} instead (CR 601.2b), so the spell costs {U}{U}{1} = 3 mana,
# exactly a Black Lotus's three blue (it sacrifices itself), and the pool is empty. Nothing is blighted: the Ornithopter has no counters. It counters a noncreature spell,
# Bot1's Mox Ruby, which goes to the graveyard (a spell of any kind is a legal target).

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Forest x19

[Bot2 Deck]
Black Lotus
Ornithopter
Wild Unraveling
Island x17

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot2.Hand.Wild Unraveling.Cast(Stack.Mox Ruby)
Bot2.Modes(Pay {1})
! Bot2.Choose
? Bot2.Mana =
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Graveyard = Mox Ruby
Bot2.Battlefield = Ornithopter
Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Counters.MinusOneMinusOne = (absent)
Bot2.Graveyard = Wild Unraveling; Black Lotus
